@@ -215,6 +215,12 @@ The [native/renderer keyboard tests](tests/keyboard.spec.ts) compile as part of
 
 Dependency installation does not run the locked Electron package's separate binary installer. Before running the [Windows console-signal tests](tests/windows-cli-signals.spec.ts) directly, prepare the locked Electron binary with `pnpm --filter @deepseek-ai/dsh-desktop exec install-electron` from the repository root. For downloads through a proxy, enable `ELECTRON_GET_USE_PROXY=1` for that installer process. Windows coverage aggregates require successful provisioning before the instrumented unit inventory starts.
 
+### Desktop main extensions
+
+Direct installed dependencies of the desktop profile can declare `"dsh": { "desktop": { "main": "./entry.js" } }` in their package manifest. Desktop imports these trusted entries after app readiness and profile preparation, before starting the Host. The entry must remain inside its package, including after symlink resolution. Installing such a plugin grants full Electron main-process authority; only install trusted packages.
+
+Export `start(api)` to receive `{ app, webContents, mainWindow, dshHome }`; `mainWindow()` returns the current primary window or `undefined`. Return a synchronous cleanup function or an object with `dispose()` to clean up on `will-quit`. Each extension's discovery, startup, and cleanup errors are logged with its package name without blocking other extensions. Restart Desktop after installing or changing extensions; hot reload is not supported. The Host environment advertises this capability as `DSH_DESKTOP_MAIN_EXTENSIONS=1`.
+
 ### Startup onboarding
 
 The API-key input starts empty and uses `autocomplete="new-password"` to ask Chromium not to autofill saved login passwords.
